# Multi-Tenant Query Standards

**CRITICAL SECURITY RULE:** Every database query MUST filter by `foundry_id` to prevent data leakage across companies.

## Quick Reference

```typescript
// ✅ ALWAYS DO THIS
const { data } = await supabase
    .from('tasks')
    .select('*')
    .eq('foundry_id', foundry_id)  // REQUIRED

// ❌ NEVER DO THIS
const { data } = await supabase
    .from('tasks')
    .select('*')  // SECURITY BREACH - No foundry filter!
```

## Multi-Tenant Tables (Require Filtering)

| Table | Filter | Exception |
|---|---|---|
| `tasks` | `.eq('foundry_id', foundry_id)` | NONE |
| `objectives` | `.eq('foundry_id', foundry_id)` | NONE |
| `teams` | `.eq('foundry_id', foundry_id)` | NONE |
| `profiles` | `.eq('foundry_id', foundry_id)` | Self-query only: `.eq('id', user.id)` |
| `messages` | Via task/objective | Need foundry_id if direct |
| `foundries` | `.eq('id', foundry_id)` | Must be user's foundry |

## Standard Pattern

```typescript
// 1. Get user's foundry_id
const { data: userProfile } = await supabase
    .from('profiles')
    .select('foundry_id')
    .eq('id', user.id)
    .single()

const foundry_id = userProfile?.foundry_id
if (!foundry_id) return <Error />

// 2. Filter ALL queries
const { data: tasks } = await supabase
    .from('tasks')
    .select('*')
    .eq('foundry_id', foundry_id)

const { data: members } = await supabase
    .from('profiles')
    .select('*')
    .eq('foundry_id', foundry_id)
```

